    "passage": "To: coolnick@emailemail.com\nFrom: customerservice@infotoday.com\nSubject: Great travel sites for your travel needs\n\nHi, Nick. This is Linda. You were asking me about some good travel websites. I would like to recommend some that I have been using lately. I like shopping for good flight deals at www.asiatravel.com, as it has some real interesting prices for airfare. When I have problem locating the flight I want, I go to www.zulu.com, where I can find the largest range of flights available.\n\nIf you are interested in getting information on a specific country, I would suggest you visit some of countries' official travel websites for the most accurate and updated information. However, I find www.travelinsights.com and www.asiainfo.com a good start to surf, as they provide some good information and tips for budget travelers.\n\nAbove all, www.traveldirectory.com has it all. All the websites mentioned above are listed here. As you mentioned about your budget trip to Shanghai, I am sure there is a suitable site for you to obtain these information.\n\nWelcome to Traveldirectory.com!\n\nVisit some of these great travel sites for your travel needs today!\n\nWeb URL\tClassification\tRemarks\n\nwww.zulu.com\tFlights / Hotels\tYou can find almost any flights available in the market here, ranging from some the cheapest to the most expensive ones. However, good deals for the American and European Sectors.\n\nwww.asiatravel.com\tFlights\tThis site will bring you good deals and promotions for air tickets. Visit this site daily for special promotions on Eastern Airlines and Japan Airlines.\n\nwww.virtualtravel.com\tFlights / Hotels / Info\tYou will find this site more informative than the good deals it offers. This site gives comprehensive coverage of travel information for most destinations. However, online booking and the purchase of airfare and hotel bookings are not as competitive.\n\nwww.travelinsights.com\tInfo Links\tYou get frank and good comments from this website. This site is good for choosing the ideal hotel. Rich in information on Japanese and South Korean hotels.\n\nwww.asiainfo.com\tInfo\tThis site mainly covers Asian destinations. It contains budget hotels and motels and is great for budget travelers.",
